# UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer suppressions.
#
# One `<check>:<file or function>` per line. Every entry here is a deliberate
# case with a reason written beside it; anything not named still fails the
# build. That is the point of keeping this file rather than dropping
# -fsanitize=integer: the flag catches unsigned overflow, which is *defined*
# behaviour and therefore something CRAN never checks, and which is still a
# bug when it happens to a length, an offset or a block count.
#
# Empty, deliberately. The vendored tree was expected to need entries --
# hash mixing and constant-time arithmetic both want wrapping -- and so far
# it has not. When one is needed, add it with a comment naming why the
# wrapping is intended, not merely that it happens.
#
# Format reference:
#   unsigned-integer-overflow:src/vendor/tf-psa-crypto/lib/sha256.c
#   shift:mbedtls_ct_uint_mask
